WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.110
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:03.739
It's question Tuesday, the day that I answer
real questions from real nerdfighters.

00:00:03.739 --> 00:00:08.889
I asked for brief questions and of course
I got them, beginning: briefs or boxers?

00:00:08.889 --> 00:00:10.349
I wear boxer briefs, lets move on!

00:00:10.349 --> 00:00:13.879
"If everybody stopped sneezing, how long do
you think it would take somebody to realize

00:00:13.879 --> 00:00:14.879
it?"

00:00:14.879 --> 00:00:15.879
Wow, I don't know.

00:00:15.879 --> 00:00:18.870
I guess I'm gonna say like a month, but I'd
like to see some rigorous research applied

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.990
to the question it's a very interesting one.

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:25.070
I think it would take a little while for people
to be like "hey, have you sneezed recently?

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:26.070
Because I haven't."

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.090
"How do you think having children has impacted
your writing?"

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:31.790
I guess there are a lot of times where 2009
me would have been writing and 2015 me is

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:33.290
making a Lego wookie gun ship.

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:37.070
But I gotta say I don't really feel like it's
a bad change, I mean this thing holds 2 different

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.500
Wookiees, it has double wookie pilots.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.270
"A girl at my school told me she'd rather
be popular than smart, what's the correct

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:43.400
response to this?"

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.400
mmmm... sympathy?

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.480
"Hey John, what's your middle name?"

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:47.480
Danger!

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:48.480
It's not.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:49.480
It's Michael.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:50.850
"Last TV show you marathoned?"

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.280
The Americans, which is excellent.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.030
"Hey, are you writing another book?"

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:56.820
You know another awesome thing about this
wookie gun ship it opens up, it's got like

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.810
a cargo bay inside of it.

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:01.059
"Who's a relatively unknown poet you love?"

00:01:01.059 --> 00:01:03.990
There's a lot but the first who comes to mind
is the Persian poet Hafiz who I feel like

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:05.970
is not as well-known here as he should be.

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:10.140
"Apart from pizza, what do you think is the
best--" No, no, no, there is no "apart from

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.140
pizza."

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:15.140
Not a lot of things in this world that make
me angry, but you should not be apart from

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:16.140
pizza.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.610
Alright, I apologize for the seriousness but
that's something I feel strongly about.

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:19.770
Let's return to lighter questions!

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.490
"Hey, I heard they're making Looking For Alaska
into a movie, who're you going to cast--"

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:25.229
I don't cast movie adaptations of my books
or actually any movies.

00:01:25.229 --> 00:01:27.610
"Hey, will you cast Katie Ho--" Yeah, I just
don't cast movies.

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:33.420
I'm a novelist and a video blogger and a pizza
enthusiast, and not a caster of films.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.460
"Hey, when are you gonna do your inkless tattoo
punishment?"

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:36.460
Soon.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:37.460
Ish.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:39.450
Maybe I should get "I don't cast movies" Tattoo'd
on my face.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:43.360
No, that's a bad idea even for an inkless
tattoo but I do need a tattoo idea, let me

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:44.580
know if you have any in comments.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:49.050
"If you could use one dinosaur to ride onto
it's back into battle, what dinosaur would

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:50.050
it be?"

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:51.050
Hey Henry?

00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:52.280
I have a dino-question for you.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:53.630
Apparently we're gonna go with Apatosaurus.

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:56.869
"Hey now that you're back home, what project
are you most excited to work on?"

00:01:56.869 --> 00:01:58.470
Well, we still haven't put the wings on.

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:01.070
I think they like flap, it's gonna be awesome
when it's finished.

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:04.790
Also, I'm signing my name over and over again
so that independent bookstores around the

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.970
US will have signed copies of Paper Towns
for the holidays.

00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:09.729
"Hey, I didn't see your cameo in the Paper
Towns movie."

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:13.000
Yeah it's not so much something you see so
much as it's someone you hear.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:18.380
And finally, "Do you think you or Hank would
get further in American Ninja Warrior."

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:21.680
Henry and I have been watching a lot of American
Ninja Warrior, so I have a built-in advantage

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:24.750
because I at least know what it is, whereas
I suspect Hank doesn't.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:28.120
I actually like my odds to get past the quintuple
steps.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.280
So yeah, I'm gonna say me.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.930
Hank, maybe we can add American Ninja Warrior
to next year's quadragicon.

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:34.210
In the meantime, I will see you on Friday.

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:37.210
Wait, I forgot to answer the most-asked question
of the week!

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:38.750
"Can we see Willie?"

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:39.750
Willie!

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:40.750
Treat!

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:41.750
Hi.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:43.430
(gurgling/babbling noises)

